"/wiki/Lae%27zel/Cinematics\" title=\"Lae'zel/Cinematics\">Cinematics</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Lae'zel</b> can be <a href=\"/wiki/Romance\" title=\"Romance\">romanced</a>. The following sections explain Lae'zel's romance-specific storyline.\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Storyline\">Storyline</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Act_One\">Act One</span></h3>\n<p>True to her personality, Lae'zel starts as forward and aggressively with romance as she does fights on the battlefield.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> She is possessive <sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>, private <sup id=\"cite_ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>, jealous <sup id=\"cite_ref-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and unwilling to share the player character with others. At first only about sex, if romance is allowed to progress, Lae'zel's perception of the player character slowly evolves, eventually seeing them as a peer, then partner; she becomes genuine, passionate and loyal in her affections towards the player character.\n</p><p>Romance with Lae'zel can begin if the player character has at least medium (20) <a href=\"/wiki/Approval\" title=\"Approval\">approval</a> with her. At this threshold, an exclamation icon [&nbsp;! ] may appear above her head after defeating one of the following enemies with Lae'zel in the party:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Hag</li>\n<li>Ogres</li>\n<li>Owlbear</li>\n<li>Spider Matriarch</li></ul>\n<p>If the player character speaks to her at this point, Lae'zel admits she misjudged them, that they have proven their courage, and bluntly states she is aroused by their scent. She then offers a night of sensual pleasure.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Manually_starting_a_romance\">Manually starting a romance</span></h4>\n<p>If the player character does not speak to Lae'zel immediately when the [&nbsp;! ] icon appears, defeats one of the listed enemies without her, or long rests at least once in the Mountain Pass or Underdark, a new dialogue option may unlock to initiate her romance: <i>\"Is it just me, or have you been looking at me differently lately?\"</i>\n</p><p>This option is only available at 20+ approval and disappears once selected. It is permanently disabled for Origin Karlach and temporarily blocked during Lae'zel’s crisis following her rejection by Vlaakith. Selecting it can lead to one of three outcomes:\n</p>\n<ol><li>If the player character is double-dating, Lae'zel dismisses the advance, stating she prefers \"fresh meat\".</li>\n<li>If the player character is partnered with someone else, Lae'zel rejects the player, noting that they have already caught someone else's eye.</li>\n<li>Otherwise, Lae'zel confesses that she misjudged the player character and they have now gained her respect and yearning.</li></ol>\n<p>The player character can agree to, decline, or mock her offer - with corresponding changes in approval. If answering by telling Lae'zel they have <i>\"been wanting a hot githyanki girlfriend\"</i>, she clarifies her intentions: <i>\"I won't be your 'girlfriend', but I 'will' be your lay. Yes or no?\"</i> Accepting starts Lae'zel's romance and flags the player as dating her.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6d/Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png/350px-Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/6d/Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png/525px-Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/6d/Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png/700px-Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Lae'zel stands at the altar room threshold, in her camp garb, inviting the player character to night of pleasure without commitment.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6d/Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png/350px-Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"197\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/6d/Lae%27zel_at_the_altar_room_threshold.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>Lae'zel stands at the altar room threshold, inviting the player character to night of pleasure without commitment.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The goblin or tiefling celebration night offers another opportunity to romance Lae'zel. She rejects the player character if they are already dating two others, or her approval of them is 19 or less.\n</p><p>If the player character agrees to her offer, Lae'zel approaches just before a long rest occurs. She tells the player character, <i>\"I've come to sate you and be sated. I lead. You follow.\"</i> The player character follows her to the altar room threshold and she soon reappears, naked. Lae'zel, aggressive and used to being in control, then demands the player character to submit.\n</p><p>A rough sexual scene occurs if any of these options are chosen:\n</p>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-transcript\">\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\">[SHADOWHEART]&nbsp;</span></span><i>Put your previous confrontation with Lae'zel out of your mind. Give in to her demand.</i></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\"></span></span><i>Close your eyes. You are hers.</i></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\"></span></span><i>Do as she asks. Taste.</i></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\">[BERSERKER]&nbsp;</span></span><b>Make me submit. SHOW ME YOUR RAGE.</b></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\">[BARBARIAN]&nbsp;</span></span>I do not submit. And I don't want submission from you. Show me your rage.</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\">[GITHYANKI]&nbsp;[HALF-ORC]&nbsp;[DRAGONBORN]&nbsp;</span></span>No. You submit to <i>me.</i> After, you can take whatever you desire.</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\">[INTIMIDATION]&nbsp;</span></span>That isn't how it's going to go. <i>You</i> submit to <i>me.</i>&nbsp;(DC 15)</span></li></ul>\n</div>\n<p>If asked what she intends to do, Lae'zel slowly saunters around the player character and answers, \"I intend to <i>take</i> my pleasure. Say the word 'no', and you will go untasted. Say <i>yes</i>, and you brave turbulent waters. Tell me.\" After this dialogue, the following options also work:\n</p>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-transcript\">\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\"></span></span>Yes. Take me.</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\">[BERSERKER]&nbsp;</span></span><b>YES.</b></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\">[BARBARIAN]&nbsp;</span></span>Yes, damn it!</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\">[GITHYANKI]&nbsp;[HALF-ORC]&nbsp;[DRAGONBORN]&nbsp;</span></span>You misunderstand. I will not submit to you, but <i>you</i> to <i>me</i>.</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-option\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-dialogue-tags\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-physical\">[INTIMIDATION]&nbsp;</span></span>You misunderstand. I will not submit to you, but <i>you</i> to <i>me</i>.&nbsp;(DC 15)</span></li></ul>\n</div>\n<p>Regardless of who takes charge, the player character wakes up next morning - aching in various places. Lae'zel insists it was just for pleasure and spends no time on sentimentality, having already begun preparing to leave camp by the time the player character starts to recover. Depending on conversation choices, the engagement may develop in future acts, with more dialogues and scenes.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bb/Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png/350px-Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/bb/Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png/525px-Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/bb/Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png/700px-Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"A picture of Lae'zel at camp. She has roused the player character from sleep at their bedside, and is looking at them with anticipation, as she eagerly awaits another night with them.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bb/Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png/350px-Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"182\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/bb/Another_night_with_Lae%27zel.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>Lae'zel, rousing the player character from sleep at their bedside, awaits another night with them.</figcaption></figure>At camp during an evening, some time after the initial sex scene, an exclamation point may appear above [!] her head. If spoken with, Lae'zel observes she has, on several occasions since their first night together, caught the player character looking at her \"with lidded eyes\" and perhaps, as she sees it, wants to sleep with her again. If agreeing with her assessment, she reminds them she never promised to be with them more than once. If agreeing but promising to stop, she deflects, answering, <i>\"I did not say it was unwelcome.\"</i> With either choice, she playfully challenges the longing player character with an offer: <i>\"Tempt me.\"</i> Any response except declining results in <a href=\"/wiki/Approval\" title=\"Approval\">approval</a> and her approaching them upon a long rest, followed by another implied sex scene which happens off-screen.\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Act_Two\">Act Two</span></h3>\n<p>Lae'zel's Act Two romance scene is unlocked when the following conditions are met: \n</p>\n<ul><li>The player is dating Lae'zel.</li>\n<li>At least one night has passed since her initial romance scene.</li>\n<li>The party has visited either Last Light Inn or Moonrise Towers.</li></ul>\n<p>One night, Lae'zel wakes the player character to confess that she is obsessed with them, and that the intensity of her feelings unsettles her. She demands a duel, insisting the player character proves their martial prowess to show they are worthy of her obsession. Accepting the duel initiates combat between the two and concludes when either party reaches sufficiently low hit points.<sup id=\"cite_ref-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Using certain potions in combat (and potentially other items such as coatings or scrolls) prompts disapproving overhead remarks from her,<sup id=\"cite_ref-9\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> but this does not affect the battle's results.<sup id=\"cite_ref-10\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\nRegardless of who wins,<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/5/55/Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png/350px-Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/5/55/Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png/525px-Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/5/55/Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png/700px-Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Lae'zel, is out of breath after being bested by the player character from her challenge to prove worthy of her affections in combat. She has a look of awe and exhaustion on her face.\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/5/55/Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png/350px-Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"182\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/5/55/Lae%27zel_-_bested_by_battle.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>Lae'zel, after being bested by the player character from her battle-challenge to prove themselves worthy of her continuing affections.</figcaption></figure> the player character has the option to progress their romance with her after the fight. If they win, she is amazed by their skill in combat, saying they are <i>\"jhe'stil.\"</i> If they lose, she finds herself still unable to dispense with her feelings and vows to protect them. In either case, she asks the player character to confirm their affection towards her; if confirmed, Lae'zel declares the player character <i>\"Zhak vo'n'ash duj.</i> Source of my bruises.\" This fully partners them with Lae'zel and ends any other ongoing affairs.\n<p>Lae'zel's romance can start anytime in Act Two if the <i>\"Is it just me, or have you been looking at me differently lately?\"</i> dialogue option is still available. If the player waits until Act 2 to initiate her romance this way, long resting in an Act 2 camp when her romance night is queued will initiate the duel scene, bypassing her first sex scene.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Act_Three\">Act Three</span></h3>\n<p>Lae'zel's Act Three romance scene unlocks one night after Vlaakith's visit. If the party long rest in the Lower City, Lae'zel wakes the player character and leads them to the rooftops. As they watch the sunrise together, she reflects on how she once despised Faerûn and everything in it, but now the player character has shown her its beauty.\n</p><p>On the Orpheus path, Lae'zel asks the player character to stay with her \"when this is all over,\" which they can accept or decline. If she remains loyal to Vlaakith, however, Lae'zel ends the relationship here, saying the player character is a distraction and that she belongs to her queen.\n</p><p>If choosing the \"Destroy the Brain\" ending, Lae'zel's story can have multiple resolutions based on decisions in several quests connected to her.\n</p><p><b>Join Orpheus into battle</b>\n</p><p>The player character can tell her to stay with them, ending the game with their romance intact, letting her fly off with <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Orpheus\" title=\"Orpheus\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e0/Portrait_Orpheus.png/25px-Portrait_Orpheus.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/e/e0/Portrait_Orpheus.png/38px-Portrait_Orpheus.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/e/e0/Portrait_Orpheus.png/50px-Portrait_Orpheus.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Orpheus\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e0/Portrait_Orpheus.png/25px-Portrait_Orpheus.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/e/e0/Portrait_Orpheus.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Orpheus\" title=\"Orpheus\">Orpheus</a> if he is alive, or join her and him to slay Vlaakith once for all. If Orpheus is a mind flayer, he wishes to commit suicide, but prior to that he asks Lae'zel to lead the Githyanki instead. If Lae'zel accepts Orpheus' request, he can be persuaded to live to see their people free. Lae'zel accepts the duty she now has and leaves to fight the battle against <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Vlaakith\" title=\"Vlaakith\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/ba/Vlaakith_Icon.webp/18px-Vlaakith_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/ba/Vlaakith_Icon.webp/26px-Vlaakith_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/ba/Vlaakith_Icon.webp/35px-Vlaakith_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Vlaakith\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/ba/Vlaakith_Icon.webp/18px-Vlaakith_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/ba/Vlaakith_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Vlaakith\" title=\"Vlaakith\">Vlaakith</a>.\n</p><p><b>Tasked to kill Orpheus by Vlaakith</b>\n</p><p>If Lae'zel remains loyal to Vlaakith after meeting Voss near the Crèche in Act 1 and after talking to Vlaakith in Act Three, she is commanded to kill Orpheus. If freed after the <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Emperor\" title=\"The Emperor\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png/25px-Portrait_The_Emperor.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png/38px-Portrait_The_Emperor.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png/50px-Portrait_The_Emperor.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Emperor\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png/25px-Portrait_The_Emperor.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/The_Emperor\" title=\"The Emperor\">Emperor</a> abandons the party due to the player character's choices, they must persuade her Orpheus is needed. After the final battle, Lae'zel tries to kill him; the player character is given the option to watch it happen, not look while it is happening or attack her. The third option immediately kills Lae'zel, while the other two result in her being sacrificed for the lich queen later on.\n</p><p><b>Emperor as Ally</b>\n</p><p>Similar to the above, if she is loyal to Orpheus and is convinced to let the Emperor assimilate him, she leaves to lead the fight against Vlaakith after everything that has happened, knowing her own duty and what will come next.<sup class=\"noexcerpt navigation-not-searchable\">[<a href=\"/wiki/bg3wiki:Verification\" title=\"bg3wiki:Verification\"><span aria-label=\"Needs verification.\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"bg3wiki-help-tooltip\"><i>verify</i></span></a>]</sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h2>\n<div class=\"notebegin\">\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r345964\">.mw-parser-output .reflist .references{list-style-type:inherit}.mw-parser-output .refs-act1::before{content:\"Act 1\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-act2::before{content:\"Act 2\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-act3::before{content:\"Act 3\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-style:italic;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-url::before{content:\"External links\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-text::before{content:\"Literature\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}.mw-parser-output .refs-note::before{content:\"Notes\";text-decoration:none;background:none;font-size:100%;font-weight:bold;direction:ltr}</style><div class=\"reflist refs-nogroup\" style=\"list-style-type:decimal;\"><div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> After spending their first night with Lae'zel, if the player character says, <i>\"Last night was wonderful, I really enjoyed myself.\"</i> Lae'zel matter-of-factly answers with, <i>\"Of course you did. I'm as extraordinary in bed as I am on the battlefield.\"</i> </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> If the player character accepts Lae'zel's offer of a night pleasure without commitments, she answers with, <i>\"Perhaps one night soon, I will come to your bunk and take what is mine.\"</i> </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> If Lae'zel is defeated in her romance-binding battle with the player character, Lae'zel pronounces, <i>\"You are 'mine'. Say the words.\"</i> </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> Once Lae'zel's relationship with the player character becomes a committed one, they can tell her they would like to kiss her. Upon hearing this, Lae'zel states incredulously, <i>\"Here? Now? If it weren't apparent, it 'should' be: I'm not keen on such 'outward' displays of our flesh-bond.\"</i> She can nevertheless be convinced to give a kiss with a successful <a href=\"/wiki/Persuasion\" title=\"Persuasion\">persuasion</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/Intimidation\" title=\"Intimidation\">intimidation</a> check. This may only be done once. </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-5\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> At the tiefling victory party after successfully defending the Emerald Grove, if the player character accepts an offer of night romance with another, Lae'zel derisively comments it is their loss they did not accept a night with her instead. </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-6\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-6\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> In Act Two, if the player character was in earlier stages of romance with Lae'zel but then bonds with Karlach during a night of intimacy (or just cuddling), they may speak with Lae'zel the following day. If spoken to, Lae'zel observes, <i>\"I see you've picked up a paramour.\"</i> The player character can answer, \"Yes. Does that bother you?\", to which she answers, <i>\"No. But it heightens my cravings for you. Not that it matters. You've made your choice. I'd only debase myself asking you to un-make it.\"</i> If replying with, <i>\"You're right - I've made my choice.\"</i> Lae'zel wryly observes, <i>\"Mm. Go. Be satisfied. And try not to think of 'me' when your 'special friend' comes to keep you company.\"</i> </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-7\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-7\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> Depending on character level, game Difficulty level, equipment and tactics used, Lae'zel may be difficult to defeat. If besting her is desired, it may be helpful to leave her with only rudimentary equipment and / or diminshed hit points prior to long rests, when combat is anticipated. </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-8\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-8\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> It is possible to <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Downed_(Condition)\" title=\"Downed (Condition)\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/66/Downed_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Downed_Condition_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/66/Downed_Condition_Icon.webp/38px-Downed_Condition_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/66/Downed_Condition_Icon.webp/50px-Downed_Condition_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"down\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/66/Downed_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Downed_Condition_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/66/Downed_Condition_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Downed_(Condition)\" title=\"Downed (Condition)\">down</a> Lae'zel if sufficient damage is done while she is on the threshold of defeat. If this happens, the player character cries out in anguished surprise, \"By the gods, not Lae'zel!\" If downed, the post combat cut-scene does not occur, the player character is automatically bonded with Lae'zel, and other romances are ended. Additionally, if allowed to die, Lae'zel must then be <a href=\"/wiki/Revivify\" title=\"Revivify\">revived</a> by spell, <a href=\"/wiki/Scrolls\" title=\"Scrolls\">scroll</a>, or with <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Withers\" title=\"Withers\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/25px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/38px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/50px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Withers\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png/25px-Portrait_Withers.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/2/25/Portrait_Withers.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Withers\" title=\"Withers\">Withers</a>. </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-9\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-9\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> Some have reported the player character's use of items in the partnering duel with Lae'zel causes loss of approval with her, while others have done the same with no loss in approval at all. Results may vary. </span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-10\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-10\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"> If Lae'zel has potions in her inventory (e.g. healing, strength, or invisibility) she uses them during her duel with the player character. </span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714194712\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.149 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.157 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 2919/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 38115/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 9358/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 22/200\nExpensive parser function count: 6/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19412/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.061/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1290483/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  130.868      1 -total\n 48.97%   64.089      1 Template:Party_interactions\n 44.17%   57.802      1 Template:Sidebar\n 13.52%   17.700     10 Template:Ref\n  9.70%   12.691      3 Template:Template_style\n  7.61%    9.956     12 Template:Dialogue_option\n  7.16%    9.375      1 Template:Reflist\n  6.91%    9.042      5 Template:Icon_link\n  6.76%    8.851      1 Template:Companion_tab\n  6.43%    8.419      5 Template:Icon_text\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pcache:idhash:19441-0!canonical and timestamp 20260714194712 and revision id 380628. Rendering was triggered because: unknown\n -->\n</div>"}